[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186221456 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc" :question/id #uuid "173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-343881" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}-2y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that all the sine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)-2(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))=2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n-2\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}-2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)=2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2} &=2 \\\\ {a}_{n}(-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}-2) &=\\frac{4(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2} &=-1 \\\\ {a}_{n} &=\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea" "answer-field-b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-58fa8e03-d7cd-5f19-b56f-8c8b5ce961c0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-58fa8e03-d7cd-5f19-b56f-8c8b5ce961c0" "answer-18978f68-c58c-5f2a-8f7b-25428043b14f" "answer-45fa900b-3979-5618-b1b9-fb89c6d62181" "answer-b3e1b4f9-d7d2-5781-9f50-427a90102375"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-58fa8e03-d7cd-5f19-b56f-8c8b5ce961c0" :answer/id #uuid "58fa8e03-d7cd-5f19-b56f-8c8b5ce961c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-18978f68-c58c-5f2a-8f7b-25428043b14f" :answer/id #uuid "18978f68-c58c-5f2a-8f7b-25428043b14f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45fa900b-3979-5618-b1b9-fb89c6d62181" :answer/id #uuid "45fa900b-3979-5618-b1b9-fb89c6d62181" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b3e1b4f9-d7d2-5781-9f50-427a90102375" :answer/id #uuid "b3e1b4f9-d7d2-5781-9f50-427a90102375" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6" :answer-field/id #uuid "b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-85fb2746-85c3-5db1-aa9e-044f72c869d2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-88f32a63-6af7-57f4-9c73-3ba79916b27f" "answer-bd764dba-88a3-5530-9aae-919254788be0" "answer-0d813839-1a92-5fef-92e3-6abd140b2570" "answer-85fb2746-85c3-5db1-aa9e-044f72c869d2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88f32a63-6af7-57f4-9c73-3ba79916b27f" :answer/id #uuid "88f32a63-6af7-57f4-9c73-3ba79916b27f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd764dba-88a3-5530-9aae-919254788be0" :answer/id #uuid "bd764dba-88a3-5530-9aae-919254788be0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0d813839-1a92-5fef-92e3-6abd140b2570" :answer/id #uuid "0d813839-1a92-5fef-92e3-6abd140b2570" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-85fb2746-85c3-5db1-aa9e-044f72c869d2" :answer/id #uuid "85fb2746-85c3-5db1-aa9e-044f72c869d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186221457 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-5451bd81-3dbb-5037-b212-6d323ecbc14d" "question-ede3a234-3946-5f25-9a03-9a90ef1ab597"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-5451bd81-3dbb-5037-b212-6d323ecbc14d" :question/id #uuid "5451bd81-3dbb-5037-b212-6d323ecbc14d" :question/math-academy-id "q-343892" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}+4{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x),$ where the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below regarding the resonant component of a particular solution of the equation.\n\nThe natural frequency of the system matches the frequency of the {{field-1}} harmonic of the forcing function. \n\nConsequently, the particular solution contains a resonant term of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}={{field-2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{4{\\pi }^{2}}=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $2$-periodic function $(L=1)$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{1}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nFor $n=2$, we have ${\\omega }_{2}=2\\pi .$ Since ${\\omega }_{2}=\\omega ,$ the $n=2$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=2$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{2}(x)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{2}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x))+x(-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{2}}^{″} & =-4\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)+4\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)-4{\\pi }^{2}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{2}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{2}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+4{\\pi }^{2}y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x):$\n\n$$\n[-4\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)+4\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)-4{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{2}}]+4{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-4\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)+4\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4\\pi A &=0 \\\\ 4\\pi B &=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A &=0 \\\\ B &=\\frac{1}{16\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}=\\frac{x}{16\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe" "answer-field-ea0c1b86-be42-5ed8-8407-44c6d02f507d"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe" :answer-field/id #uuid "f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-4a0c32ad-de23-5e9f-808f-1f78006c64f1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5905e0f3-5309-5e10-b501-239325d54809" "answer-4a0c32ad-de23-5e9f-808f-1f78006c64f1" "answer-536818d9-9dbd-5964-9c9f-aa017860190d" "answer-f3502541-53e5-5a9c-82ae-a11a00feb7b5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5905e0f3-5309-5e10-b501-239325d54809" :answer/id #uuid "5905e0f3-5309-5e10-b501-239325d54809" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4a0c32ad-de23-5e9f-808f-1f78006c64f1" :answer/id #uuid "4a0c32ad-de23-5e9f-808f-1f78006c64f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-536818d9-9dbd-5964-9c9f-aa017860190d" :answer/id #uuid "536818d9-9dbd-5964-9c9f-aa017860190d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f3502541-53e5-5a9c-82ae-a11a00feb7b5" :answer/id #uuid "f3502541-53e5-5a9c-82ae-a11a00feb7b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea0c1b86-be42-5ed8-8407-44c6d02f507d" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea0c1b86-be42-5ed8-8407-44c6d02f507d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-16a06cdf-1029-5b2d-8051-f494a395997b" :answer-field/choices ["answer-5e9e39c5-6e2a-58a4-93e5-d6d8d1b2f101" "answer-16a06cdf-1029-5b2d-8051-f494a395997b" "answer-36d09d73-8dc7-558b-93a5-9c8ae8216ec7" "answer-2860517c-57e1-51b2-9dbc-fee215b2642a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5e9e39c5-6e2a-58a4-93e5-d6d8d1b2f101" :answer/id #uuid "5e9e39c5-6e2a-58a4-93e5-d6d8d1b2f101" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{16\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-16a06cdf-1029-5b2d-8051-f494a395997b" :answer/id #uuid "16a06cdf-1029-5b2d-8051-f494a395997b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{16\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-36d09d73-8dc7-558b-93a5-9c8ae8216ec7" :answer/id #uuid "36d09d73-8dc7-558b-93a5-9c8ae8216ec7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{32\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2860517c-57e1-51b2-9dbc-fee215b2642a" :answer/id #uuid "2860517c-57e1-51b2-9dbc-fee215b2642a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{x}{8\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186222040 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-ede3a234-3946-5f25-9a03-9a90ef1ab597" :question/id #uuid "ede3a234-3946-5f25-9a03-9a90ef1ab597" :question/math-academy-id "q-343912" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}y=f(x),$ where the $4$-periodic forcing function is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below regarding the resonant component of a particular solution of the equation.\n\nThe natural frequency of the system matches the frequency of the {{field-1}} harmonic of the forcing function. \n\nConsequently, the particular solution contains a resonant term of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}={{field-2}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $4$-periodic function $(L=2)$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{2}.\n$$\n\nFor $n=3$, we have ${\\omega }_{3}=\\frac{3\\pi }{2}.$ Since ${\\omega }_{3}=\\omega ,$ the $n=3$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=3$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{3}(x)=\\frac{8}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{3}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}))+x(-\\frac{3\\pi }{2}A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+\\frac{3\\pi }{2}B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{3}}^{″} & =-3\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+3\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{3}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{3}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}y=\\frac{8}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}):$\n\n$$\n[-3\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+3\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})-\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}{y}_{{p}_{3}}]+\\frac{9{\\pi }^{2}}{4}{y}_{{p}_{3}}=\\frac{8}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-3\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})+3\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})=\\frac{8}{9}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3\\pi A &=\\frac{8}{9} \\\\ 3\\pi B &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A &=-\\frac{8}{27\\pi } \\\\ B &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{3}}=-\\frac{8x}{27\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2}).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-a9e19625-804c-5b01-89fe-15a44c087d3b" "answer-field-24a1b253-dea2-5722-80f3-4ed1534482dc"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a9e19625-804c-5b01-89fe-15a44c087d3b" :answer-field/id #uuid "a9e19625-804c-5b01-89fe-15a44c087d3b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-e3410172-077c-5b4c-b1c5-73dcfaebadb1" :answer-field/choices ["answer-46ab8f72-a107-5264-917d-17e7a0db3bc8" "answer-a65673dc-f1f0-522a-bafe-68ef7278ee0c" "answer-e3410172-077c-5b4c-b1c5-73dcfaebadb1" "answer-8e2eb7fd-63ac-5bde-a164-58af1a7b608b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46ab8f72-a107-5264-917d-17e7a0db3bc8" :answer/id #uuid "46ab8f72-a107-5264-917d-17e7a0db3bc8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a65673dc-f1f0-522a-bafe-68ef7278ee0c" :answer/id #uuid "a65673dc-f1f0-522a-bafe-68ef7278ee0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3410172-077c-5b4c-b1c5-73dcfaebadb1" :answer/id #uuid "e3410172-077c-5b4c-b1c5-73dcfaebadb1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8e2eb7fd-63ac-5bde-a164-58af1a7b608b" :answer/id #uuid "8e2eb7fd-63ac-5bde-a164-58af1a7b608b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "n=4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-24a1b253-dea2-5722-80f3-4ed1534482dc" :answer-field/id #uuid "24a1b253-dea2-5722-80f3-4ed1534482dc" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "answer-3d5cbe55-beb8-55d8-b3d7-1b0220ae60dc" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c3be416c-5de9-5416-9071-8b9539a10c79" "answer-3ddbd52d-d970-5293-adcd-958e5e7719b2" "answer-3d5cbe55-beb8-55d8-b3d7-1b0220ae60dc" "answer-d76ab2b6-88a5-5b3a-a528-1ec41b175396"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c3be416c-5de9-5416-9071-8b9539a10c79" :answer/id #uuid "c3be416c-5de9-5416-9071-8b9539a10c79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{16x}{27\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3ddbd52d-d970-5293-adcd-958e5e7719b2" :answer/id #uuid "3ddbd52d-d970-5293-adcd-958e5e7719b2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{27\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d5cbe55-beb8-55d8-b3d7-1b0220ae60dc" :answer/id #uuid "3d5cbe55-beb8-55d8-b3d7-1b0220ae60dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{8x}{27\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d76ab2b6-88a5-5b3a-a528-1ec41b175396" :answer/id #uuid "d76ab2b6-88a5-5b3a-a528-1ec41b175396" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{8x}{27\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi x}{2})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-7a6e0e2d-aea3-57b8-9349-dc6403d4a565" :activity/id #uuid "7a6e0e2d-aea3-57b8-9349-dc6403d4a565" :activity/title "Solving ODEs Using Fourier Series" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049288 :activity/course 17592186046673 :activity/steps ["step-01f60ef7-8079-5daa-8af1-84aed6eb94d9" "step-2056cf6d-97e5-5b4c-8fe6-3ed4e8245ff6" "step-17d1c9c7-0cfe-56bd-9b51-f5c9dc90e176" "step-874a9c11-68e1-5999-a104-d6e0019eb1a9" "step-cc70b6b4-c1e8-52da-a137-2fea2d22b608"] :activity/first-step "step-01f60ef7-8079-5daa-8af1-84aed6eb94d9" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-01f60ef7-8079-5daa-8af1-84aed6eb94d9" :step/id #uuid "01f60ef7-8079-5daa-8af1-84aed6eb94d9" :step/content 17592186317448 :step/next "step-2056cf6d-97e5-5b4c-8fe6-3ed4e8245ff6" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-2056cf6d-97e5-5b4c-8fe6-3ed4e8245ff6" :step/id #uuid "2056cf6d-97e5-5b4c-8fe6-3ed4e8245ff6" :step/content "question-173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc" :step/next "step-17d1c9c7-0cfe-56bd-9b51-f5c9dc90e176" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-17d1c9c7-0cfe-56bd-9b51-f5c9dc90e176" :step/id #uuid "17d1c9c7-0cfe-56bd-9b51-f5c9dc90e176" :step/content "question-5451bd81-3dbb-5037-b212-6d323ecbc14d" :step/next "step-874a9c11-68e1-5999-a104-d6e0019eb1a9" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-874a9c11-68e1-5999-a104-d6e0019eb1a9" :step/id #uuid "874a9c11-68e1-5999-a104-d6e0019eb1a9" :step/content 17592186222040 :step/next "step-cc70b6b4-c1e8-52da-a137-2fea2d22b608" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cc70b6b4-c1e8-52da-a137-2fea2d22b608" :step/id #uuid "cc70b6b4-c1e8-52da-a137-2fea2d22b608" :step/content "question-ede3a234-3946-5f25-9a03-9a90ef1ab597" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc" :question/id #uuid "173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc"] ["question-173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-343881"] ["question-173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc" :question/problem "Select the missing parts in a particular solution of the differential equation ${y}^{″}-2y=f(x),$ where the Fourier series of the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that all the sine coefficients in the Fourier series of the particular solution are equal to zero.*\n\nThe Fourier series of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼{{field-1}}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,{{field-2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\n$$"] ["question-173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc" :question/worked-solution "We assume that a solution of our equation has the following Fourier series:\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{p}^{′} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x) \\\\ {y}_{p}^{″} & ∼\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}n\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(n\\pi x))∼{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{p}^{″}$ and ${y}_{p}$ into the equation and have\n\n$$\n{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-{a}_{n}{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)-2(\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x))=2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get \n\n$$\n-2\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}(-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}-2)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x)=2+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{4(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the free terms and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2\\cdot \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2} &=2 \\\\ {a}_{n}(-{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}-2) &=\\frac{4(-1)^{n+1}}{{n}^{3}\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2} &=-1 \\\\ {a}_{n} &=\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{p}∼-1+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$"] ["question-173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea"] ["answer-58fa8e03-d7cd-5f19-b56f-8c8b5ce961c0" :answer/id #uuid "58fa8e03-d7cd-5f19-b56f-8c8b5ce961c0"] ["answer-58fa8e03-d7cd-5f19-b56f-8c8b5ce961c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-58fa8e03-d7cd-5f19-b56f-8c8b5ce961c0" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-18978f68-c58c-5f2a-8f7b-25428043b14f" :answer/id #uuid "18978f68-c58c-5f2a-8f7b-25428043b14f"] ["answer-18978f68-c58c-5f2a-8f7b-25428043b14f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-18978f68-c58c-5f2a-8f7b-25428043b14f" :answer/value "-2"] ["answer-45fa900b-3979-5618-b1b9-fb89c6d62181" :answer/id #uuid "45fa900b-3979-5618-b1b9-fb89c6d62181"] ["answer-45fa900b-3979-5618-b1b9-fb89c6d62181" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-45fa900b-3979-5618-b1b9-fb89c6d62181" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-b3e1b4f9-d7d2-5781-9f50-427a90102375" :answer/id #uuid "b3e1b4f9-d7d2-5781-9f50-427a90102375"] ["answer-b3e1b4f9-d7d2-5781-9f50-427a90102375" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b3e1b4f9-d7d2-5781-9f50-427a90102375" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-field-fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select] ["answer-field-fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea" :answer-field/correct "answer-58fa8e03-d7cd-5f19-b56f-8c8b5ce961c0"] ["answer-field-fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea" :answer-field/choices "answer-58fa8e03-d7cd-5f19-b56f-8c8b5ce961c0"] ["answer-field-fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea" :answer-field/choices "answer-18978f68-c58c-5f2a-8f7b-25428043b14f"] ["answer-field-fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea" :answer-field/choices "answer-45fa900b-3979-5618-b1b9-fb89c6d62181"] ["answer-field-fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea" :answer-field/choices "answer-b3e1b4f9-d7d2-5781-9f50-427a90102375"] ["answer-field-b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6" :answer-field/id #uuid "b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6"] ["answer-88f32a63-6af7-57f4-9c73-3ba79916b27f" :answer/id #uuid "88f32a63-6af7-57f4-9c73-3ba79916b27f"] ["answer-88f32a63-6af7-57f4-9c73-3ba79916b27f" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-88f32a63-6af7-57f4-9c73-3ba79916b27f" :answer/value "-\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}"] ["answer-bd764dba-88a3-5530-9aae-919254788be0" :answer/id #uuid "bd764dba-88a3-5530-9aae-919254788be0"] ["answer-bd764dba-88a3-5530-9aae-919254788be0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bd764dba-88a3-5530-9aae-919254788be0" :answer/value "\\frac{(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}"] ["answer-0d813839-1a92-5fef-92e3-6abd140b2570" :answer/id #uuid "0d813839-1a92-5fef-92e3-6abd140b2570"] ["answer-0d813839-1a92-5fef-92e3-6abd140b2570" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0d813839-1a92-5fef-92e3-6abd140b2570" :answer/value "\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}"] ["answer-85fb2746-85c3-5db1-aa9e-044f72c869d2" :answer/id #uuid "85fb2746-85c3-5db1-aa9e-044f72c869d2"] ["answer-85fb2746-85c3-5db1-aa9e-044f72c869d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-85fb2746-85c3-5db1-aa9e-044f72c869d2" :answer/value "\\frac{4(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}\\pi ({n}^{2}{\\pi }^{2}+2)}"] ["answer-field-b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select] ["answer-field-b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6" :answer-field/correct "answer-85fb2746-85c3-5db1-aa9e-044f72c869d2"] ["answer-field-b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6" :answer-field/choices "answer-88f32a63-6af7-57f4-9c73-3ba79916b27f"] ["answer-field-b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6" :answer-field/choices "answer-bd764dba-88a3-5530-9aae-919254788be0"] ["answer-field-b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6" :answer-field/choices "answer-0d813839-1a92-5fef-92e3-6abd140b2570"] ["answer-field-b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6" :answer-field/choices "answer-85fb2746-85c3-5db1-aa9e-044f72c869d2"] ["question-173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-fdd2be53-eb30-5618-9f90-b3ba36d2b3ea"] ["question-173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b655e2b6-7bed-525a-9b08-edcf720fdfc6"] [17592186221456 :knowledge-point/questions "question-173f7026-2304-5e9a-9c5d-ccb6401619bc"] ["question-5451bd81-3dbb-5037-b212-6d323ecbc14d" :question/id #uuid "5451bd81-3dbb-5037-b212-6d323ecbc14d"] ["question-5451bd81-3dbb-5037-b212-6d323ecbc14d" :question/math-academy-id "q-343892"] ["question-5451bd81-3dbb-5037-b212-6d323ecbc14d" :question/problem "Consider the differential equation ${y}^{″}+4{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x),$ where the $2$-periodic forcing function is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼3+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(n\\pi x).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below regarding the resonant component of a particular solution of the equation.\n\nThe natural frequency of the system matches the frequency of the {{field-1}} harmonic of the forcing function. \n\nConsequently, the particular solution contains a resonant term of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}={{field-2}}.\n$$"] ["question-5451bd81-3dbb-5037-b212-6d323ecbc14d" :question/worked-solution "We begin by identifying resonance. The differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+4{\\pi }^{2}y=f(x)\n$$\n\nhas a natural frequency of \n\n$$\n\\omega =\\sqrt{4{\\pi }^{2}}=2\\pi .\n$$\n\nThe frequencies of the forcing harmonics for a $2$-periodic function $(L=1)$ are \n\n$$\n{\\omega }_{n}=\\frac{n\\pi }{1}=n\\pi .\n$$\n\nFor $n=2$, we have ${\\omega }_{2}=2\\pi .$ Since ${\\omega }_{2}=\\omega ,$ the $n=2$ harmonic of the forcing function causes resonance.\n\nFor the $n=2$ harmonic, the forcing term is \n\n$$\n{f}_{2}(x)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x).\n$$\n\nBecause this frequency matches the natural frequency, we assume a particular solution of the form\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}=x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)).\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{{p}_{2}}^{′} & =(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x))+x(-2\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)+2\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)) \\\\ {y}_{{p}_{2}}^{″} & =-4\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)+4\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)-4{\\pi }^{2}x(A\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)+B\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the expressions for ${y}_{{p}_{2}}^{″}$ and ${y}_{{p}_{2}}$ into the equation ${y}^{″}+4{\\pi }^{2}y=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x):$\n\n$$\n[-4\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)+4\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)-4{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{2}}]+4{\\pi }^{2}{y}_{{p}_{2}}=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)\n$$\n\nThe resonant terms involving $x$ cancel out, leaving\n\n$$\n-4\\pi A\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x)+4\\pi B\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x)=\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\pi x).\n$$\n\nNow, equating the sine and cosine coefficients, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-4\\pi A &=0 \\\\ 4\\pi B &=\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}A &=0 \\\\ B &=\\frac{1}{16\\pi }\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the resonant component of a particular solution is\n\n$$\n{y}_{{p}_{2}}=\\frac{x}{16\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\pi x).\n$$"] ["question-5451bd81-3dbb-5037-b212-6d323ecbc14d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe" :answer-field/id #uuid "f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe"] ["answer-5905e0f3-5309-5e10-b501-239325d54809" :answer/id #uuid "5905e0f3-5309-5e10-b501-239325d54809"] ["answer-5905e0f3-5309-5e10-b501-239325d54809" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-5905e0f3-5309-5e10-b501-239325d54809" :answer/value "n=1"] ["answer-4a0c32ad-de23-5e9f-808f-1f78006c64f1" :answer/id #uuid "4a0c32ad-de23-5e9f-808f-1f78006c64f1"] ["answer-4a0c32ad-de23-5e9f-808f-1f78006c64f1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-4a0c32ad-de23-5e9f-808f-1f78006c64f1" :answer/value "n=2"] ["answer-536818d9-9dbd-5964-9c9f-aa017860190d" :answer/id #uuid "536818d9-9dbd-5964-9c9f-aa017860190d"] ["answer-536818d9-9dbd-5964-9c9f-aa017860190d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-536818d9-9dbd-5964-9c9f-aa017860190d" :answer/value "n=3"] ["answer-f3502541-53e5-5a9c-82ae-a11a00feb7b5" :answer/id #uuid "f3502541-53e5-5a9c-82ae-a11a00feb7b5"] ["answer-f3502541-53e5-5a9c-82ae-a11a00feb7b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f3502541-53e5-5a9c-82ae-a11a00feb7b5" :answer/value "n=4"] ["answer-field-f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select] ["answer-field-f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe" :answer-field/correct "answer-4a0c32ad-de23-5e9f-808f-1f78006c64f1"] ["answer-field-f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe" :answer-field/choices "answer-5905e0f3-5309-5e10-b501-239325d54809"] ["answer-field-f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe" :answer-field/choices "answer-4a0c32ad-de23-5e9f-808f-1f78006c64f1"] ["answer-field-f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe" :answer-field/choices "answer-536818d9-9dbd-5964-9c9f-aa017860190d"] ["answer-field-f61c11e2-3120-5201-9414-72b0b0528efe" :answer-field/choices "answer-f3502541-53e5-5a9c-82ae-a11a00feb7b5"] 